                                "example_id": "627f9027-45e4-4364-8cd5-f171e158fcbb",
                                "sense_id": "aeb10c24-44d5-3679-aa7a-ee461196ab2e",
                                "text": "ARMAGEDDON, a name occurring in the Authorized Version of the English Bible in Rev. xvi. 16. The Revised Version has Harmagedon. The form is commonly regarded as the Greek equivalent of the Hebrew har megiddōn, the mountain district of Megiddo. The writer is describing the place where the last decisive battle was to be fought at the Day of Judgment, and Harmagedon may have been chosen as the name because the district about Megiddo had been on several occasions the scene of great battles."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
